{
  "dom_id": "step-q338291",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Consider the function $y=\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}.$  Find the derivative of $y.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | $(x+2)^{3}\\,(-5{x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{2}\\,+$ \n{{field-2}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | ${({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{4}$ |",
  "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((x+2)^{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}+2x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}+2x-1)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+2}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+2x-1}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+2) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{4}{x+2}-\\frac{3(3{x}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{3}+2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{4}{x+2}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{3}+2x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{4}{x+2}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{3}+2x-1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}(\\frac{4}{x+2}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{3}+2x-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}(\\frac{4({x}^{3}+2x-1)-(x+2)(9{x}^{2}+6)}{(x+2)({x}^{3}+2x-1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{3}}(\\frac{-5{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+2x-16}{(x+2)({x}^{3}+2x-1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{3}(-5{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+2x-16)}{{({x}^{3}+2x-1)}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
